      "text": "To compute the sum \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor + \\cdots + \\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\rfloor\\), we need to find the floor value of the square root of each integer from 1 to 16 and sum those values.\n\nWe start by calculating the exact value of each square root and then find the floor value:\n\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1 \\rfloor = 1\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1.414 \\rfloor = 1\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1.732 \\rfloor = 1\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{4} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2 \\rfloor = 2\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{5} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.236 \\rfloor = 2\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{6} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.449 \\rfloor = 2\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{7} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.646 \\rfloor = 2\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{8} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.828 \\rfloor = 2\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{9} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3 \\rfloor = 3\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{10} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.162 \\rfloor = 3\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{11} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.317 \\rfloor = 3\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{12} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.464 \\rfloor = 3\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{13} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.606 \\rfloor = 3\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{14} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.742 \\rfloor = 3\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{15} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.873 \\rfloor = 3\\)\n- \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 4 \\rfloor = 4\\)\n\nNow we sum these values:\n\n\\[\n1 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 4 = 27\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{27}\n\\]",
