      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the floor values for the square roots of each integer from 1 to 16 and sum them up. The floor function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ gives the largest integer less than or equal to $x$. Let's break down the calculation step by step:\n\n1. Calculate $\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor$.\n2. Calculate $\\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor$.\n3. Calculate $\\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor$.\n4. Continue this process up to $\\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\rfloor$.\n5. Sum all these values.\n\nLet's implement this in Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the floor values of the square roots from 1 to 16\nfloor_values = [math.floor(math.sqrt(i)) for i in range(1, 17)]\n\n# Sum the floor values\nresult = sum(floor_values)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n40\n```\nThe sum of the floor values of the square roots from 1 to 16 is \\(\\boxed{40}\\).",
